WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:06.839
Since it aired in 2003, NCIS has had so many
storylines and characters that it can be a

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.390
bit jarring to go back to the first season.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:13.800
So, let's take a few moments and remember
a few of the forgotten things from the first

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.610
season of NCIS.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.160
Let's go back to the very beginning.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:22.390
No, we're not talking about "Yankee White,"
the first episode of season one we're going

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:28.070
all the way back to "Ice Queen," the episode
of the legal drama JAG, which first introduced

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.210
Gibbs, Abby, Tony, and Ducky.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.210
"Is that number two or three today?"

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.220
"If you must know it's number four."

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.360
"Brought you a little present."

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:43.940
The characters appeared on two episodes of
JAG that served as a backdoor pilot for NCIS,

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.500
which was conceived as an investigative crime
drama series in the same universe.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:54.200
Vivian "Viv" Blackadder was a former FBI agent,
with an incredible name, who was working for

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.090
NCIS before the events of the first season.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:02.460
In the two backdoor pilot episodes, Viv was
shown to be a determined, but clumsy, agent.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.689
Despite being a central player during the
backdoor pilot, the character of Viv never

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:08.509
made the leap to the main series.

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:14.969
According to an oral history of NCIS on TV
Insider, series co-creator Donald P. Bellisario

00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:19.119
thought the character was too soft and decided
to nix her from the show.

00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:23.770
While Vivian may be a character that you missed
out on seeing, don't worry - there are plenty

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.929
of other familiar faces that you'd recognize
today.

00:01:26.929 --> 00:01:31.289
The first season of the show is full of guest
appearances from actors who went on to become

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:33.479
very well-known TV stars.

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:38.750
In the episode "Enigma," Terry O'Quinn plays
Gibbs' former commanding officer, who disappears

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.770
with millions of dollars of Saddam Hussein's
money.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:46.670
Josh Holloway has a smaller role as a cocky
local sheriff who gets on Gibbs' bad side

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.880
on the episode "My Other Left Foot."

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.600
Dean Norris from Breaking Bad also makes an
appearance in the same episode as a Marine

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.859
Corps sergeant.

00:01:54.859 --> 00:02:00.350
In the episode "Split Decision," Scandal star
Bellamy Young plays an ATF agent who gets

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.240
swept up in an NCIS investigation.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.700
Switching back to the main cast, Agent Tim
McGee is one of the longest-running characters

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.120
on NCIS, but the character wasn't supposed
to last more than one episode.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.250
Lucky for him, he caught the eye of viewers
and producers during the first season and

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.500
eventually became a series regular.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.720
One of the McGee storylines that was most
endearing was his budding relationship with

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.720
Abby.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.780
The two hit it off almost as soon as McGee
arrived on the scene, but starting in the

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.470
second season, their relationship started
to fizzle.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.879
There were a few hints that suggested the
two were still hooking up occasionally, but

00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:39.540
their flirtatious banter eventually died out
and the relationship was mostly forgotten

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.819
by the show.

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:44.750
One of the biggest things you'll notice when
revisiting season one, you'll notice that

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:49.340
several of the personalities of the show's
long-running characters have evolved quite

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.340
a bit.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.730
One example is how Gibbs' gruff, but fun,
personality -

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.508
"Well don't dismiss me like that.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.611
Ok I earned my jock strap."

00:02:57.611 --> 00:02:58.375
"Yeah?

00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:00.726
Does it ever give you that empty feeling?"

00:03:00.726 --> 00:03:01.726
"What?"

00:03:01.726 --> 00:03:03.150
"Your jock strap."

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.600
- became more serious and somber as the show
went on.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:11.709
Another is how Abby's bubbly charms were turned
up to the extreme in later seasons, versus

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:15.530
the quirky, but cool, tone she set at the
beginning of the show's run.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:20.750
Both of these could be considered examples
of "Flanderization," a common television trend

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.700
where a show takes an action or trait of a
character and exaggerates it more and more

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.010
until other personality subtleties are lost.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.460
Or it's just that the characters evolved.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.460
Up to you.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.769
For an example of that, take a look at Tony.

00:03:34.769 --> 00:03:38.409
In the first few seasons his personality was
like that of a frat boy -

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:40.989
"Sweeeet!"

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:44.819
or as dearly departed NCIS Agent Kate Todd
once called him -

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:46.939
"An X-Rated Peter Pan."

00:03:46.939 --> 00:03:51.740
While Tony is still a bit of a cad during
later seasons, he matured quite a bit over

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.450
the years and mostly left his penchant for
inappropriate workplace jokes behind him.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:01.860
Those are just some things that might surprise
you during a rewatch of NCIS's early days.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:06.719
With season 18 beginning in late 2020, there's
no better time to go back and see where it

00:04:06.719 --> 00:04:08.269
all began.

